### API Testing File for VS Code REST Client Extension
### Install the "REST Client" extension to use this file

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000
@contentType = application/json

### Health Check
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health

### Root Endpoint
GET {{baseUrl}}/

### Test 1: Signup - Valid User
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "firstName": "John",
  "lastName": "Doe",
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "company": "Test Company",
  "industry": "pharmaceutical",
  "password": "SecurePass123!",
  "agreedToTerms": true
}

### Test 2: Signup - Duplicate Email (Should Fail)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "firstName": "Jane",
  "lastName": "Doe",
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "company": "Another Company",
  "industry": "biotechnology",
  "password": "AnotherPass123!",
  "agreedToTerms": true
}

### Test 3: Signup - Invalid Email Format (Should Fail)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "firstName": "Test",
  "lastName": "User",
  "email": "invalid-email",
  "industry": "healthcare",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "agreedToTerms": true
}

### Test 4: Signup - Short Password (Should Fail)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "firstName": "Test",
  "lastName": "User",
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "industry": "agriculture",
  "password": "Pass1!",
  "agreedToTerms": true
}

### Test 5: Signup - Terms Not Agreed (Should Fail)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "firstName": "Test",
  "lastName": "User",
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "industry": "pharmaceutical",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "agreedToTerms": false
}

### Test 6: Login - Valid Credentials
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "password": "SecurePass123!"
}

### Test 7: Login - Invalid Password
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "password": "WrongPassword"
}

### Test 8: Login - Non-existent User
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "nonexistent@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### Test 9: Get Current User Profile (Replace TOKEN with actual token from login)
@authToken = YOUR_TOKEN_HERE

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

